        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758308,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Nintendo Game Boy Advance (GBA), released in 2001, was a pivotal handheld console, succeeding the Game Boy Color and ushering in a new era of portable gaming. This 32-bit powerhouse boasted a more powerful ARM7 processor and improved graphics, while maintaining backward compatibility with older Game Boy titles. It quickly became a global phenomenon, selling over 81 million units. \n\nThe GBA’s library was diverse, ranging from platformers and SNES-like RPGs to ports of classic 8-bit and 16-bit games. Popular titles like *Pokémon Ruby and Sapphire* captivated players worldwide. Unique features like rumble, tilt, and solar sensors added innovative gameplay elements. Later models, including the SP and Micro, offered enhanced designs and features. The GBA’s legacy continues, with digital re-releases on Nintendo’s online services, ensuring its enduring appeal."
          },
